SuperTux (apps/supertux)

Game (engine/)
  SuperTux 0.7.0, by the SuperTux Development Team and contributors.
  License: GNU General Public License, version 3 or later
  (engine/LICENSE.txt).
  Source: https://github.com/SuperTux/supertux, release v0.7.0
  (SuperTux-v0.7.0-Source.tar.gz), with frunk.store's changes for the
  browser in engine/supertux-web.patch (also tools/supertux/supertux-web.patch
  in https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose
  tools/build-supertux.mjs builds it). The patched source the build came
  from, without the data folder (published as is in data/, see below), is
  engine/supertux-0.7.0-web-src.tar.gz.
  The changes: the game's main loop waits for the page's next animation
  frame inside main(), with JSPI, instead of Emscripten's main loop, so a
  frame can also wait for the game's files, which the page reads on demand;
  WebAssembly exceptions instead of Emscripten's JavaScript ones (JSPI
  can't wait across JavaScript frames); the data is mounted by the page at
  /data rather than preloaded; PhysicsFS gets a program path, which it
  can't look up on the web; the page says whether to show the on-screen
  controls; no Add-ons, Manage Assets or Donate entries on the title menu
  (no add-on downloads, file uploads or outside links in the car); the
  Emscripten ports the build uses stand in for vcpkg's packages; and the
  version is set to v0.7.0.
  Built with the menus SuperTux uses on phones (HIDE_NONMOBILE_OPTIONS: no
  level editor, resolution or cursor options) and without networking.

  Libraries compiled into it:
  - PhysicsFS 3.2.0, by Ryan C. Gordon and contributors: zlib license.
    Source: engine/physfs-3.2.0.tar.gz (https://github.com/icculus/physfs).
  - {fmt} 11.2.0, by Victor Zverovich and contributors: MIT license.
    Source: engine/fmt-11.2.0.tar.gz (https://github.com/fmtlib/fmt).
  - GLM 1.0.1, by G-Truc Creation: MIT license (The Happy Bunny license
    also offered). Source: engine/glm-1.0.1.tar.gz (https://github.com/g-truc/glm).
  - In SuperTux's own source tree (external/): SDL_ttf, tinygettext and
    SDL_SavePNG (zlib), Squirrel, SimpleSquirrel and findlocale (MIT),
    sexp-cpp (GPL-3.0), obstack (LGPL-2.1, from the GNU C Library) and
    partio_zip (BSD 3-Clause).
  - Emscripten's ports: SDL2, SDL2_image, libpng, zlib, FreeType, libogg
    and libvorbis, under their own licenses (zlib, libpng, FreeType
    Project License, BSD), and Emscripten's runtime (MIT and
    University of Illinois/NCSA).

Data (data/)
  SuperTux 0.7.0's data folder, unchanged, from the same release: the
  levels, worlds, scripts, art, music, sounds, fonts and translations by
  the SuperTux artists, musicians, level designers and translators, under
  the GPL (version 2 or 3 or later), Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
  and Attribution, and other free licenses, file by file as data/LICENSES.txt
  (the game's AUTHORS, ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS.txt and credits) records; the fonts
  are under the SIL Open Font License or Apache License 2.0 (data/*LICENSE*).
  It is packed for streaming by tools/supertux/pack.mjs: the files one
  after another (in the order data/index.json lists them, with their sizes)
  cut into 1 MB blocks, data/<version>/<n>.bin, some gzipped (.bin.gz).
  Joining the blocks in order (ungzipping the .gz ones) and cutting the
  result by the sizes in index.json gives back every file.

